# SRG-APP-000855-AU-000340  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must for password-based authentication, require
# immediate selection of a new password upon account recovery.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000855-AU-000340
group:           V-263578
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004063
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    None that bears on account recovery: Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 has no
                 setting that marks a password as reset and forces its replacement at next
                 login. The nearest adjacent setting, authentication.conf [splunk_auth]
                 forceWeakPasswordChange, makes users replace a password that fails the
                 current complexity rules, which is keyed on weakness rather than on
                 recovery, and the product offers no self-service password recovery to
                 configure.

external:        The account recovery procedure, including requiring the user to select a
                 new password immediately after an administrator reset - carried by the
                 organization's account-management procedure.
external:        Where authType is LDAP, SAML, or ProxySSO, recovery and the forced change
                 at next login are performed by the directory service or identity provider.

manual_reason:   No conf key represents account recovery or a change-at-next-login
                 obligation, so no observed configuration value can decide this
                 requirement.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:509 (forceWeakPasswordChange,
                 default false - weak-password replacement, not recovery); no recovery or
                 change-at-next-login key exists in [splunk_auth] at :437-600
finding:         Not a finding against the application: Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 has no
                 setting that forces selection of a new password upon account recovery, so
                 this requirement is carried by the organization's account-management
                 procedure and by the directory service or identity provider where
                 authentication is external; this determination is from the perspective of
                 the application layer alone.
